          "lineNumber": 110,
          "lineContent": "case event := \u003c-h.broadcast:",
          "title": "Event Broadcasting",
          "description": "Hub event loop receives broadcast events and distributes to all registered clients"
        },
        {
          "id": "3f",
          "path": "packages/gui/src/api/hooks.ts",
          "lineNumber": 238,
          "lineContent": "queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: [\"jobs\"] });",
          "title": "Query Invalidation",
          "description": "Event handler invalidates relevant queries causing automatic refetch of stale data"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "SSE Real-time Update Flow\n│\n├── Frontend: React Component\n│   ├── Layout mounts \u003c-- packages/gui/src/api/hooks.ts:232\n│   │   └── useSSE() hook called \u003c-- 3a\n│   │       └── subscribeToEvents() \u003c-- packages/gui/src/api/client.ts:326\n│   │           └── new EventSource() \u003c-- 3b\n│   │               └── GET /api/events\n│   │\n│   └── Event received\n│       └── onmessage handler \u003c-- packages/gui/src/api/client.ts:332\n│           └── invalidateQueries() \u003c-- 3f\n│\n└── Backend: Go Web Server\n    ├── Route registration\n    │   └── mux.HandleFunc() \u003c-- 3c\n    │       └── sse.Handler() \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/sse/handler.go:12\n    │\n    ├── Client connection\n    │   └── hub.Register() \u003c-- 3d\n    │       └── client added to hub.clients \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/sse/hub.go:97\n    │\n    └── Event broadcasting\n        └── h.broadcast channel \u003c-- 3e\n            └── broadcastEvent() \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/sse/hub.go:111\n                └── client.Send \u003c- msg \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/sse/hub.go:191\n                    └── w.Write() to EventSource \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/sse/handler.go:67",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe GUI needs to stay synchronized with backend state changes without constantly polling. When jobs complete, tasks update, or agents change state, the frontend must **immediately reflect these changes** across all open browser tabs. Server-Sent Events (SSE) provides a lightweight, unidirectional push mechanism where the Go backend can broadcast invalidation events to all connected React clients, triggering automatic data refetches only when necessary.\n\n## Details\n\n### Frontend Connection\n\nThe React app establishes an SSE connection during layout initialization [3a]. The `useSSE()` hook creates an **EventSource** pointing to `/api/events` [3b], which maintains a persistent HTTP connection. This hook runs once when the Layout component mounts, ensuring all pages benefit from real-time updates.\n\nWhen events arrive, the `onmessage` handler parses the event type and calls `queryClient.invalidateQueries()` [3f] for the relevant query keys (e.g., \"jobs\", \"tasks\"). TanStack Query then **automatically refetches** any active queries matching those keys, updating the UI without manual intervention.\n\n### Backend Broadcasting\n\nThe Go web server registers the `/api/events` endpoint with an SSE handler [3c] that upgrades incoming HTTP connections to streaming responses. Each connection creates a client with a buffered send channel and registers it with the central SSE hub [3d].\n\nThe hub runs an event loop that listens on a broadcast channel [3e]. When backend operations (job completion, task updates) need to notify clients, they publish events to this channel. The hub's `broadcastEvent()` function marshals events to JSON and writes them to all registered client channels [3e], which are then flushed to the HTTP response streams.\n\n### Key Design Points\n\n- **No polling overhead**: Clients maintain a single long-lived connection instead of repeatedly hitting endpoints\n- **Automatic invalidation**: The frontend doesn't need to know what changed, just which query keys to refresh\n- **Multi-tab support**: All browser tabs receive the same events and stay synchronized\n- **Graceful degradation**: If SSE fails, the app still works via manual refresh or navigation"
    },
    {
