        },
        {
          "id": "4c",
          "path": "internal/interfaces/web/server.go",
          "lineNumber": 91,
          "lineContent": "mux.HandleFunc(\"/ws/console/\", consolews.HandleWebSocket(s.consoleHub, s.log))",
          "title": "WebSocket Route",
          "description": "Server registers /ws/console/ endpoint with WebSocket handler and console hub"
        },
        {
          "id": "4d",
          "path": "internal/interfaces/web/consolews/hub.go",
          "lineNumber": 184,
          "lineContent": "conn, err := websocket.Accept(w, r, \u0026websocket.AcceptOptions{",
          "title": "WebSocket Upgrade",
          "description": "Handler upgrades HTTP connection to WebSocket with origin validation"
        },
        {
          "id": "4e",
          "path": "internal/interfaces/web/consolews/hub.go",
          "lineNumber": 176,
          "lineContent": "session = hub.CreateSession(SessionConfig{",
          "title": "Session Creation",
          "description": "Hub creates or retrieves console session with workspace and profile configuration"
        },
        {
          "id": "4f",
          "path": "internal/interfaces/web/consolews/session.go",
          "lineNumber": 236,
          "lineContent": "if err := runner.Run(reqCtx, s, p.Content, correlationID); err != nil {",
          "title": "Message Processing",
          "description": "Session handles ask payload by running LLM request with user message and correlation ID"
        },
        {
          "id": "4g",
          "path": "internal/interfaces/web/consolews/session.go",
          "lineNumber": 164,
          "lineContent": "s.Broadcast(NewEventPayload(s.id, correlationID, content, metadata))",
          "title": "Response Broadcast",
          "description": "Session broadcasts streaming events and replies to all connected WebSocket clients"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Console WebSocket Session Flow\n├── Frontend: ConsolePage Component\n│   └── useConsoleWebSocket() hook call \u003c-- 4a\n│       └── WebSocket connection setup\n│           └── new WebSocket(wsUrl) \u003c-- 4b\n│\n├── Backend: Web Server Routes\n│   └── /ws/console/ route registration \u003c-- 4c\n│       └── HandleWebSocket() handler \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/consolews/hub.go:155\n│           ├── websocket.Accept() upgrade \u003c-- 4d\n│           └── Session management\n│               ├── CreateSession() \u003c-- 4e\n│               └── Client registration \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/consolews/hub.go:199\n│                   └── readPump() / writePump() \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/consolews/hub.go:202\n│\n└── Session: Message Processing\n    ├── HandlePayload() receives message \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/consolews/hub.go:225\n    │   └── handleAsk() processes user input \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/consolews/session.go:176\n    │       └── runner.Run() executes LLM \u003c-- 4f\n    │           └── Broadcast() sends response \u003c-- 4g\n    │               └── All clients receive events \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/consolews/session.go:146",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe **Console WebSocket system** enables real-time, interactive chat sessions between the GUI and backend LLM agents. Users need to send questions to AI agents and receive streaming responses without page refreshes or polling. The system maintains **persistent bidirectional connections** where multiple browser clients can connect to the same console session, see each other's messages, and receive streaming AI responses as they're generated [4g].\n\n## Details\n\n### Frontend Connection\n\nThe `ConsolePage` component uses the `useConsoleWebSocket` hook [4a] to establish a **WebSocket connection** to a specific session ID [4b]. The hook manages connection state (connected, connecting, error), message history, and provides functions to send messages and cancel in-flight requests. When a user types a message and hits send, it's transmitted over the WebSocket with a correlation ID for tracking.\n\n### Backend Session Management\n\nThe Go web server registers a `/ws/console/` endpoint [4c] that **upgrades HTTP connections to WebSocket** using the `websocket.Accept()` function with origin validation [4d]. If a session doesn't exist for the requested ID, the hub **auto-creates one** with workspace and profile configuration [4e]. Each WebSocket client is registered with the session, and two goroutines are spawned: `readPump()` for receiving messages and `writePump()` for sending responses.\n\n### Message Processing Flow\n\nWhen a client sends an \"ask\" payload (user message), the session's `HandlePayload()` function routes it to `handleAsk()`, which adds the message to conversation history and invokes the **LLM runner** in a background goroutine [4f]. The runner can stream partial responses by calling `BroadcastEvent()`, and sends the final complete response via `BroadcastReply()` [4g]. The broadcast mechanism sends messages to **all connected clients** for that session, enabling multi-client collaboration.\n\n### Cancellation and Persistence\n\nEach session maintains a cancellable context for the current in-flight request. Users can cancel long-running requests via a \"cancel\" command. The system includes a `PersistenceAdapter` that asynchronously saves session metadata and conversation turns to disk, allowing sessions to be resumed later."
    },
