        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Web Server Startup Flow\n├── cmd/agentctl_web/main.go\n│   ├── main() entry point \u003c-- cmd/agentctl_web/main.go:38\n│   │   ├── config.LoadCached() \u003c-- cmd/agentctl_web/main.go:55\n│   │   ├── web.NewServer() call \u003c-- 5a\n│   │   ├── go srv.Run(ctx) \u003c-- 5c\n│   │   ├── http.Server creation \u003c-- cmd/agentctl_web/main.go:82\n│   │   │   └── Handler: srv.Handler() \u003c-- 5e\n│   │   └── httpSrv.ListenAndServe() \u003c-- 5f\n│   └── signal handling \u0026 shutdown \u003c-- cmd/agentctl_web/main.go:105\n│\n└── internal/interfaces/web/server.go\n    ├── NewServer() initialization \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:26\n    │   ├── sse.NewHub() creation \u003c-- 5b\n    │   ├── consolews.NewHub() creation \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:28\n    │   └── return Server instance \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:42\n    │\n    └── Handler() route registration \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:61\n        ├── http.NewServeMux() \u003c-- 5d\n        ├── register /api/jobs endpoint \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:71\n        ├── register /api/events (SSE) \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:68\n        ├── register /ws/console/* \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:91\n        ├── register all other API routes\n        └── apply CORS + logging \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:152",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe foxctl web server needs to **start up reliably** and **expose multiple communication channels** to the frontend GUI. The system must support traditional REST APIs for data queries, Server-Sent Events (SSE) for real-time push notifications, and WebSocket connections for bidirectional console sessions. The startup sequence must initialize these subsystems in the correct order, register all HTTP routes, and begin listening for connections—all while handling graceful shutdown.\n\n## Details\n\n### Entry Point and Configuration\n\nThe server starts in `cmd/agentctl_web/main.go` [5a], which loads the foxctl configuration including paths to jobs, CAS storage, and database settings. This configuration is passed to all handlers that need to access persistent data.\n\n### Server Initialization\n\n`web.NewServer()` creates the core server instance with three key components:\n\n1. **SSE Hub** [5b] - A goroutine-based event broadcaster that maintains connected clients and distributes invalidation events when data changes\n2. **Console Hub** - Manages WebSocket sessions for interactive console communication\n3. **HTTP Handler** - A multiplexer that routes requests to appropriate handlers\n\nThe SSE hub is immediately started in a background goroutine [5c] so it can begin accepting client registrations before the HTTP server starts listening.\n\n### Route Registration\n\nThe `Handler()` method [5d] creates an `http.ServeMux` and registers all endpoints:\n\n- **REST APIs** like `/api/jobs` for querying job data\n- **SSE endpoint** at `/api/events` for real-time updates\n- **WebSocket endpoint** at `/ws/console/*` for console sessions\n- **Static file serving** (optional) for production deployments\n\nRoutes are registered with handler functions that receive the config and logger, enabling them to access storage and emit structured logs.\n\n### HTTP Server Start\n\nThe HTTP server is configured [5e] with the handler and appropriate timeouts (note: `WriteTimeout` is 0 to support long-lived SSE connections). The server begins listening on port 8090 by default [5f], blocking until shutdown is requested.\n\n### Graceful Shutdown\n\nSignal handlers catch SIGTERM/SIGINT, cancel the context (stopping the SSE hub), and call `httpSrv.Shutdown()` with a 5-second timeout to drain in-flight requests."
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "title": "Development Proxy Configuration",
      "description": "Local development setup - Vite dev server proxies /api and /ws requests to Go backend, enabling hot reload while maintaining API connectivity",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "6a",
          "path": "packages/gui/vite.config.ts",
          "lineNumber": 15,
          "lineContent": "proxy: {",
          "title": "Vite Proxy Config",
          "description": "Vite development server configured to proxy API and WebSocket requests"
        },
        {
          "id": "6b",
          "path": "packages/gui/vite.config.ts",
          "lineNumber": 17,
          "lineContent": "target: \"http://localhost:8090\",",
          "title": "API Proxy Target",
          "description": "All /api/* requests proxied to Go backend running on port 8090"
        },
        {
          "id": "6c",
          "path": "packages/gui/vite.config.ts",
          "lineNumber": 21,
          "lineContent": "target: \"ws://localhost:8090\",",
          "title": "WebSocket Proxy",
          "description": "WebSocket connections at /ws/* upgraded and proxied to backend"
        },
        {
          "id": "6d",
          "path": "packages/gui/package.json",
          "lineNumber": 9,
          "lineContent": "\"dev:all\": \"concurrently npm run server npm run dev\"",
          "title": "Concurrent Dev Script",
          "description": "Package script runs both Go server and Vite dev server simultaneously"
        },
        {
          "id": "6e",
          "path": "internal/interfaces/web/server.go",
          "lineNumber": 168,
          "lineContent": "w.Header().Set(\"Access-Control-Allow-Origin\", origin)",
          "title": "CORS Middleware",
          "description": "Development CORS middleware allows localhost:5173 origin for Vite dev server"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Development Environment Setup\n├── Vite Dev Server (localhost:5173)\n│   ├── vite.config.ts configuration \u003c-- packages/gui/vite.config.ts:6\n│   │   ├── proxy.\"/api\" config \u003c-- 6a\n│   │   │   └── target: localhost:8090 \u003c-- 6b\n│   │   └── proxy.\"/ws\" config \u003c-- packages/gui/vite.config.ts:20\n│   │       └── ws target: localhost:8090 \u003c-- 6c\n│   └── package.json scripts \u003c-- packages/gui/package.json:6\n│       └── dev:all runs both servers \u003c-- 6d\n│\n└── Go Backend Server (localhost:8090)\n    ├── HTTP request arrives\n    │   └── CORS middleware intercepts \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:162\n    │       └── Set Allow-Origin header \u003c-- 6e\n    └── Routes registered \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:62\n        ├── /api/* endpoints \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:71\n        └── /ws/* WebSocket endpoints \u003c-- internal/interfaces/web/server.go:91",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen developing a React SPA with a Go backend, you need to run **two separate servers**: the Vite dev server (for hot module reload) on port 5173 and the Go API server on port 8090. Without proper configuration, the frontend cannot communicate with the backend due to **CORS restrictions** and **different origins**. The development proxy setup [6a-6e] solves this by making Vite transparently forward API and WebSocket requests to the Go server, allowing seamless local development.\n\n## Details\n\n### Vite Proxy Configuration\n\nThe `vite.config.ts` file [6a] configures Vite's dev server to **proxy specific paths** to the backend:\n\n- **API requests** (`/api/*`) are forwarded to `http://localhost:8090` [6b], so frontend code can call `/api/jobs` and it reaches the Go server\n- **WebSocket connections** (`/ws/*`) are upgraded and proxied to `ws://localhost:8090` [6c], enabling real-time console sessions\n\nThis means frontend code uses **relative paths** like `/api/jobs` without hardcoding the backend URL.\n\n### Running Both Servers\n\nThe `package.json` defines a `dev:all` script [6d] that uses `concurrently` to start both the Go backend (`npm run server` which calls `foxctl web serve --dev-cors`) and the Vite dev server simultaneously. This is the **single command** developers run for local development.\n\n### CORS Handling\n\nThe Go server's CORS middleware [6e] detects the development environment and sets `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` headers to allow requests from `localhost:5173`. Without this, the browser would block API calls even with the proxy, since the WebSocket upgrade and some requests need explicit CORS approval.\n\n### Route Registration\n\nThe Go server registers all endpoints [6a] including REST APIs at `/api/*` and WebSocket handlers at `/ws/*`. The proxy ensures these routes are accessible from the frontend running on a different port."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "title": "Production Static File Serving",
      "description": "Production deployment - Go server optionally serves built React files from dist directory, falling back to API routes",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "7a",
          "path": "packages/gui/package.json",
          "lineNumber": 10,
          "lineContent": "\"build\": \"tsc -b \u0026\u0026 vite build\",",
          "title": "Build Script",
          "description": "TypeScript compilation and Vite build produces optimized static files in dist/"
        },
        {
          "id": "7b",
          "path": "cmd/foxctl/cmd/web.go",
          "lineNumber": 59,
          "lineContent": "webServeCmd.Flags().StringVar(\u0026webUIDir, \"ui-dir\", \"\", \"Directory containing static UI files to serve\")",
          "title": "UI Directory Flag",
          "description": "CLI command accepts --ui-dir flag to specify built UI files location"
        },
        {
          "id": "7c",
          "path": "internal/interfaces/web/server.go",
          "lineNumber": 130,
          "lineContent": "if s.opts.UIDir != \"\" {",
          "title": "Static Serving Check",
          "description": "Server conditionally enables static file serving if UIDir option is provided"
        },
        {
          "id": "7d",
          "path": "internal/interfaces/web/server.go",
          "lineNumber": 131,
          "lineContent": "fs := http.FileServer(http.Dir(s.opts.UIDir))",
          "title": "FileServer Creation",
